{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-3","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-3","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.md","line":29,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.tex#def:dc-ch1-2-3","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-2]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.tex","label":"def:dc-ch1-2-3","line":51,"source":"\\begin{definition}[local isometry]\n  \\label{def:dc-ch1-2-3}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch1-2-1, def:dc-ch1-2-2}\n\n  \\dcref{ch1:2.3}\n  A differentiable map $f:M\\to N$ between Riemannian manifolds is a\n  \\emph{local isometry at} $p\\in M$ if some neighborhood $U$ of $p$ is mapped\n  diffeomorphically onto $f(U)$ and the restriction satisfies (1). The manifold\n  $M$ is \\emph{locally isometric} to $N$ if every $p\\in M$ has such a neighborhood.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[local isometry] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a64632d6368312d322d33\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_RiemannianMetrics%23def%3Adc-ch1-2-1\">↗ def:dc-ch1-2-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_RiemannianMetrics%23def%3Adc-ch1-2-2\">↗ def:dc-ch1-2-2</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch1:2.3</span></span>A differentiable map <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f:M\\to N$\">$f:M\\to N$</span> between Riemannian manifolds is a <em>local isometry at</em> <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> if some neighborhood <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$U$\">$U$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> is mapped diffeomorphically onto <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f(U)$\">$f(U)$</span> and the restriction satisfies (1). The manifold <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is <em>locally isometric</em> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N$\">$N$</span> if every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> has such a neighborhood. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-2","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#ex:dc-ch1-2-4","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-1","label":"def:dc-ch1-2-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-2","label":"def:dc-ch1-2-2"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-4-2-geodesic-push","title":"lem:dc-ch8-4-2-geodesic-push","label":"lem:dc-ch8-4-2-geodesic-push"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-4-2","title":"lem:dc-ch8-4-2","label":"lem:dc-ch8-4-2"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-3","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-3","tex":"\\begin{definition}[local isometry]\n  \\label{def:dc-ch1-2-3}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch1-2-1, def:dc-ch1-2-2}\n\n  \\dcref{ch1:2.3}\n  A differentiable map $f:M\\to N$ between Riemannian manifolds is a\n  \\emph{local isometry at} $p\\in M$ if some neighborhood $U$ of $p$ is mapped\n  diffeomorphically onto $f(U)$ and the restriction satisfies (1). The manifold\n  $M$ is \\emph{locally isometric} to $N$ if every $p\\in M$ has such a neighborhood.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-1","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-1","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_RiemannianMetrics#def:dc-ch1-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch1-2-2","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}